from ./Cli import Cli
from ./Config import Config
from ./Errors import Errors
from ./OutputSize import OutputSize
from ./PngOutput import PngOutput
from ./SvgOutput import SvgOutput

export anchor Preview:
    description:
        Preview mode shows a project's compositions in a viewer that updates
        by itself whenever a source file is saved. It is started with
        `emul preview`, as described in @{Cli}.

    viewer:
        The viewer is a native desktop window built with egui, the Rust
        immediate-mode GUI library, so it ships inside the `emul` binary with
        nothing else to install. The window lists every composition exported
        from the entry file in a side panel, and shows the selected one in
        the main area.

    formats:
        - svg
            The window draws the composition from the same rendering that
            @{SvgOutput} writes, rasterized to fit the window.
        - png
            The window shows the exact image @{PngOutput} would write, at its
            configured scale, so pixel-level detail can be checked.
        - html
            egui can't render HTML, so the HTML view opens in the default web
            browser instead. `emul preview` serves it from a small local web
            server, and the browser page reloads by itself on every rebuild,
            the same as the window. A button in the window opens it.

        The window can switch between the SVG and PNG views at any time, or
        show them side by side.

    autoRefresh:
        Emul watches every `.emul` file in the project, every image it uses,
        and `emul.config.pi`. When any of them is saved, it rebuilds what
        changed and the window redraws straight away. The selected
        composition, view, zoom and scroll position are kept.

    errors:
        When a save leaves the project with errors, the window keeps showing
        the last good rendering, with the errors listed in a panel over it,
        as described in @{Errors}. Clicking an error shows its file and line.
        The view goes back to normal as soon as the errors are fixed. The
        browser page shows the same errors.

    size:
        Each composition is rendered at its size from @{OutputSize}. The
        window can zoom in and out, and fit the canvas to the window, without
        changing that size. The size flags of `emul build` also work with
        `emul preview`, to try a composition at another size.

    nothingWritten:
        Preview mode renders in memory. It does not write to the output
        directory set in @{Config}; `emul build` does that.

    flags:
        - port
            `--port <number>` sets the port the HTML view is served on.
            Defaults to `4400`, or the next free port.
        - html
            `--html` also opens the HTML view in the browser at start-up.
